
  Release Notes for 0.4.0

 o FEATURE: Structured full text: where a paper is open access, its
            JATS XML is fetched from Europe PMC and stored beside the
            PDF. A "JATS" chip on the card shows which papers have it,
            and a menu item backfills the whole library

 o FEATURE: Reference lists now come from the stored JATS rather than
            being recovered from the page — exact entries, and a DOI
            for most of them, so following a citation needs no search

 o FEATURE: Viewer: the sentence a citation was made in is shown in
            the reference popover ("Cited here as:")

 o FEATURE: Viewer: back-navigation after a citation jump, and
            text-based citation links for PDFs whose publisher left
            no link annotations

 o FEATURE: Viewer: where a paper has JATS, its citations are found
            from the publisher's own markup rather than recognised
            on the page. This is what makes citations clickable in
            papers that print them as bare superscript numerals —
            Protein Science among them — where there is nothing on
            the page to recognise

 o FEATURE: DOI-first metadata: a DOI that resolves supplies the
            record even when the PDF's own text disagrees. The
            disagreement is flagged on the card ("Check metadata")
            rather than silently applied, and papers whose DOI could
            not be confirmed are marked "Unverified"

 o FEATURE: DOIs derived from publisher download filenames — Elsevier
            PII, arXiv, bioRxiv, Nature/BMC/Springer, RSC, ACS, PNAS
            and Science

 o FEATURE: "Find metadata" in the metadata editor: type a citation
            you can read off the paper ("Jones et al., JMB, 1995")
            and pick from a ranked list of candidates. For older
            papers whose PDFs carry no usable metadata

 o FEATURE: Supporting information is recognised as a supplement and
            linked to its parent paper, with an "SI" chip, rather
            than impersonating the paper and occupying its DOI

 o FEATURE: Papers can carry a summary, written by hand or by an AI
            assistant through the MCP server. Always shown with the
            person or model that wrote it, and never mistakable for
            the abstract

 o FEATURE: MCP: set_summary and summary_overview tools, and summary
            fields on the read tools, so a connected assistant can
            see what has been summarised and write summaries back

 o FEATURE: Subscriptions flag articles written by authors you have
            looked up before, matched on ORCID or OpenAlex ID

 o FEATURE: The Authors window opens from the main menu, uses a
            navigation split view, and opens papers you already hold

 o CHANGE:  Clicking an author's name on a card opens them in the
            Authors window; filtering the library by that author
            moved to its own icon

 o CHANGE:  Feed cards render publisher markup (italics, super- and
            subscripts, small caps) instead of showing the tags

 o BUG-FIX: Bulk import no longer freezes the window. Importing a
            folder of 185 PDFs went from multi-minute stalls — the
            worst measured at nine minutes — to a worst case of a few
            seconds. Six separate faults: a database connection
            shared across threads, background sweepers rebuilding the
            card list directly, unbounded rebuild frequency,
            redundant per-card work, and concurrent PDF extractions
            competing for the interpreter

 o BUG-FIX: The weekly refresh of the PDB accession-code list no
            longer freezes an import: 57 MB was downloaded and parsed
            inline. It now runs in the background and streams

 o BUG-FIX: One import notification per file, rather than one per
            filesystem event

 o BUG-FIX: macOS AppleDouble files (._*) are no longer imported as
            if they were PDFs

 o BUG-FIX: Applying a filter reveals the search bar, so a narrowed
            list is explained and can be cleared

 o BUG-FIX: Embedded terminal: readable text in light mode, and it
            follows a light/dark switch

