  Release Notes for 0.2.0

 o FEATURE: PDB accession codes mentioned in a paper are shown on its
            card, linked to PDBe, with "Open in Coot" on right-click
            and drag-and-drop into Coot

 o FEATURE: Discover: find a paper by PDB accession code

 o FEATURE: Import from DOI: paste a DOI, fetch the metadata, and
            fetch the open-access PDF where there is one

 o FEATURE: MCP server, so an AI assistant you already use can search
            and read the library: search, find by DOI, paper records,
            sidecars, PDF text, recently added, and a one-hop
            citation neighbourhood

 o FEATURE: Embedded terminal pane (hamburger → Toggle terminal),
            with the library's environment already set

 o FEATURE: "Funded by" line on each card, from OpenAlex funders and
            awards, with a per-grant popover

 o FEATURE: Multiple catalogues: separate libraries with their own
            directories and databases

 o FEATURE: Licence and open-access chips on cards, from CrossRef,
            with an OpenAlex fallback

 o FEATURE: Crossmark chip flagging publisher-deposited corrections
            and retractions

 o FEATURE: Preprint chips, and a link to the published version when
            OpenAlex knows of one

 o FEATURE: Citation sparklines on cards, and Citation Classic stars

 o FEATURE: About dialog, application icon, and a desktop-file
            installer

 o FEATURE: macOS application bundle, so the Dock shows the icon

 o CHANGE:  The Python package and environment variables were renamed
            from pdforg to alexandria

 o CHANGE:  Sidecars renamed to <paper>.pdf.alexandria, with existing
            libraries migrated in place on first run

 o CHANGE:  Small-caps in titles rendered properly, rather than shown
            as markup

 o BUG-FIX: Background workers each open their own database
            connection, fixing the intermittent "another row
            available" failures and a crash on macOS

 o BUG-FIX: The database filename is per-host, so a shared home
            directory on NFS cannot collide

 o BUG-FIX: CrossRef rate-limit headers are honoured before a refusal
            rather than after

 o BUG-FIX: Sidecars that appear from outside the application are
            reported rather than imported blindly
